-- Regulation W, 12 CFR 223.41, 223.42 and 223.16(c): what each kind of exemption leaves in force.
--
-- Target compiler: main (see NOTES.md).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `regwb-nouns`

-- 223.41: "The following transactions are not subject to the quantitative limits of §§ 223.11 and 223.12 or the collateral
-- requirements of § 223.14. The transactions are, however, subject to the safety and soundness requirement of § 223.13 and
-- the prohibition on the purchase of a low-quality asset of § 223.15."
-- 223.42: "The following transactions are not subject to the quantitative limits of §§ 223.11 and 223.12, the collateral
-- requirements of § 223.14, or the prohibition on the purchase of a low-quality asset of § 223.15. The transactions are,
-- however, subject to the safety and soundness requirement of § 223.13."
-- 223.16(c): "the following transactions are not subject to the quantitative limits of §§ 223.11 and 223.12 or the collateral
-- requirements of § 223.14. The transactions are, however, subject to the safety and soundness requirement of § 223.13 and the
-- market terms requirement and other provisions of subpart F".  223.16(c) does not mention 223.15, so it leaves it as it is
-- (NOTES.md); every transaction it describes is an extension of credit, to which 223.15 does not apply.
-- 223.13 applies to "any covered transaction, including any transaction exempt under this regulation".
GIVEN
    e IS AN `Exemption claimed`
    r IS A Requirement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@ref 12 CFR 223.41
@ref 12 CFR 223.42
@ref 12 CFR 223.16(c)
@ref 12 CFR 223.13
`requirement still applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF r EQUALS `The safety and soundness requirement of 223.13` THEN TRUE
        IF e EQUALS `No exemption` THEN TRUE
        IF e EQUALS `An exemption under 223.41` THEN r EQUALS `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`
        IF e EQUALS `An exemption under 223.42` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE r EQUALS `The low-quality asset prohibition of 223.15`
